-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_strings.pcpp - Lexical compliance: string and character literals

  Strings follow C++ (BNF.md sec 9): adjacent literals join into one; the
  escapes are C++'s (decoded as clang does); a raw string R"(...)" keeps
  its text as written, with a delimiter when the text holds )"; L"..." is
  a wstring (the prefix touches the quote); 'c' is a char, L'w' a wchar.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\lex_strings.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\lex_strings.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    joined in one
    quote["] back[\]
    hex A octal A ucn é
    raw \n stays
    has )" inside
    wide
    c w
    len 3
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    lex_strings_err_unterminated.pcpp
      a string with no closing quote (LX0001)
    lex_strings_err_raw.pcpp
      a raw string with no closing )" (LX0002)
    lex_strings_err_delimiter.pcpp
      a raw string delimiter longer than 16 characters (LX0010)
    lex_strings_err_escape.pcpp
      an octal escape above 255 (PR0009)
    lex_strings_err_unknown_escape.pcpp
      an escape C++ does not know (PR0021, a warning: the text keeps a q)
    lex_strings_err_unknown_escape_char.pcpp
      the same in a character literal (PR0064, a warning: the character is q)
    lex_strings_err_multichar.pcpp
      a character literal of several characters (PR0064, a warning: an int32)
    lex_strings_err_char.pcpp
      an empty character literal (PR0054)
    lex_strings_err_print_prefix.pcpp
      printing a u8 string: no std::formatter (SM0425, named as written)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_strings;

begin
  println("{}", "joined " "in" " one");
  println("{}", "quote[\"] back[\\]");
  println("{}", "hex \x41 octal \101 ucn \u00e9");
  println("{}", R"(raw \n stays)");
  println("{}", R"tag(has )" inside)tag");
  println("{}", L"wide");
  println("{} {}", 'c', L'w');
  println("len {}", len("a\nb"));
end.
